lla_oneidensis)\nciteturn43search11 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 months ago; Here we used biological force microscopy (BFM) in combination with two-dimensional (2D) gel electrophoresis and protein mass spectrometry to look for evidence of inducible proteins produced exclusively to mediate contact with a specific mineral. ... This natural affinity between S. oneidensis and goethite is, presumably, a vestige of the strong evolutionary linkage between dissimila- tory metal reducing bacteria and ferric minerals. materials and methods Bacteria, Media, and Minerals S. oneidensis MR-1 (ATCC 700550) was purchased from the American Type Culture Collection (Manassas, VA) and cultured at 22 to 25°C and pH ⬃7.4 in defined M1 medium (Myers and Nealson, 1988).\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nList of minerals named after people (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_minerals_named_after_people)\nciteturn43search16 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 weeks ago; *  \"Wolfeite: Mineral information, data and localities\". ... *  \"Wroewolfeite: Mineral information, data and localities\".\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nWolfeit (https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wolfeit)\nciteturn43search17 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 6 months ago; Die Erstbeschreibung erfolgte 1949 durch Clifford Frondel, der das Mineral nach dem amerikanischen Kristallographen Professor Caleb Wroe Wolfe (1908–1980) benannte. ... * Webmineral - Wolfeite\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nWolfeite (https://it.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wolfeite)\nciteturn43search18 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last year; * (EN) Wolfeite Mineral Data, su webmineral.com, David Barthelmy.\n",
